## ✅ Problem

Print a given **name `n` times** using **recursion**.

***

## ✅ Core Idea

*   **Base case** → Stop when `n == 0`
*   **Recursive case** → Print name once, then call for `n-1`

***

## ✅ Java Solution (Most Common in Interviews)

```java
public class PrintNameRecursion {

    static void printName(String name, int n) {
        // Base case
        if (n == 0) {
            return;
        }

        // Print name
        System.out.println(name);

        // Recursive call
        printName(name, n - 1);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        printName("Yuvan", 5);
    }
}
```

### ✅ Output

    Yuvan
    Yuvan
    Yuvan
    Yuvan
    Yuvan

***

## ✅ Dry Run (n = 3)

    printName("Yuvan", 3)
    → prints Yuvan
    → printName("Yuvan", 2)

    printName("Yuvan", 2)
    → prints Yuvan
    → printName("Yuvan", 1)

    printName("Yuvan", 1)
    → prints Yuvan
    → printName("Yuvan", 0)

    printName("Yuvan", 0)
    → return (base case)

***

## ✅ Recursion Tree

    printName(3)
      |
    printName(2)
      |
    printName(1)
      |
    printName(0)  ← base case

***

## ✅ Time & Space Complexity

| Metric        | Complexity |
| ------------- | ---------- |
| Time          | **O(n)**   |
| Space (stack) | **O(n)**   |

***

## ✅ Common Interview Variant

**Print name in reverse order**

```java
static void printReverse(String name, int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;

    printReverse(name, n - 1);
    System.out.println(name);
}
```

Output is still printed `n` times, but **after recursion returns**.

***

