## ✅ What is Multiple Recursion?

✅ **Multiple recursion** means a function makes **more than one recursive call** inside itself.

📌 Fibonacci is the **classic example** of multiple recursion.

***

## ✅ Fibonacci Definition

**Fibonacci sequence**:

    0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, ...

### Mathematical Formula

    fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)

This leads to **two recursive calls** → hence **multiple recursion**.

***

## ✅ Fibonacci Using Multiple Recursion (Java)

```java
public class Fibonacci {

    static int fib(int n) {
        // Base cases
        if (n == 0) return 0;
        if (n == 1) return 1;

        // Multiple recursive calls
        return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 5;
        System.out.println(fib(n));
    }
}
```

### ✅ Output

    5

***

## ✅ Why This Is Multiple Recursion?

```java
return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
```

➡️ **Two recursive calls in one function**

*   `fib(n - 1)`
*   `fib(n - 2)`

Hence → **Multiple recursion**

***

## ✅ Dry Run (fib(4))

    fib(4)
     = fib(3) + fib(2)

    fib(3)
     = fib(2) + fib(1)

    fib(2)
     = fib(1) + fib(0)

Evaluate bottom‑up:

    fib(2) = 1
    fib(1) = 1
    fib(3) = 2
    fib(4) = 3

***

## ✅ Recursion Tree for fib(4)

                   fib(4)
                 /        \
            fib(3)        fib(2)
            /    \        /     \
       fib(2)  fib(1)  fib(1)  fib(0)
       /    \
    fib(1) fib(0)

### Observations ✅

*   Same subproblems repeated
*   Tree grows exponentially
*   Leads to poor performance

***

## ✅ Base Cases (Very Important)

```java
if (n == 0) return 0;
if (n == 1) return 1;
```

✅ These stop recursion  
❌ Without them → **stack overflow**

***

## ✅ Time & Space Complexity

### Time Complexity

*   **O(2ⁿ)** ❌ (Exponential)
*   Due to repeated calls

### Space Complexity

*   **O(n)** ✅ (Recursion stack depth)

***

## ✅ Why This Approach Is Inefficient?

*   `fib(2)` computed multiple times
*   `fib(1)` computed many times
*   Wastes time & stack memory

